From: Linexa Engineering <linexa@fem.linexa>
Date: 2026-08-04
Subject: [PATCH] Fix proot-me/proot#182: readlinkat(fd, "", ...) empty-pathname abort

Linexa independent proot build fix. The tracee-side readlinkat() exit
handler re-reads the translated pathname argument; when the pathname is
empty (kernel-legal since Linux 2.6.39: the *at syscall then operates on
dirfd itself), the empty string was passed as the referrer to
detranslate_path(), which runs compare_paths("/proc", "") -> path.c
compare_paths2(path_length=0) -> assert(length2 > 0) -> SIGABRT
(upstream proot-me/proot#182, still open; PR #415 unmerged).

The guard below is the semantically-correct handling of the empty
pathname: resolve the referrer through /proc/<pid>/fd/<dirfd> instead of
handing "" to detranslate_path(). This is a byte-equivalent backport of
the well-tested termux/proot fix (commit c79069fc, 2020-10-17,
termux/proot#123) which is shipped in termux proot 5.1.107-68.

Upstream status at time of writing (2026-08-04): latest release v5.4.0
still lacks this guard; proot-me/proot#182 open; PR #415 open/unmerged.

NDEBUG is deliberately NOT used: it would demote the assert to the
PATHS_ARE_NOT_COMPARABLE fallback, leaving the host target visible as a
guest path (path-leak/correctness bug) and strip future asserts.

Regression test: test/test-readlinkat-empty-pathname.c (see
jniLibs/proot-build/test-readlinkat-empty-pathname.c)

diff --git a/src/syscall/exit.c b/src/syscall/exit.c
index 70dce99..1d47a92 100644
--- a/src/syscall/exit.c
+++ b/src/syscall/exit.c
@@ -361,6 +361,19 @@
 			break;
 		}
 
+		if (status == 1) {
+			/* Empty path was passed (""),
+			 * indicating that path is pointed to by fd passed in first argument */
+			word_t dirfd = peek_reg(tracee, ORIGINAL, SYSARG_1);
+			if (syscall_number == PR_readlink || dirfd < 0) {
+				status = -EBADF;
+				break;
+			}
+			status = readlink_proc_pid_fd(tracee->pid, dirfd, referer);
+			if (status < 0)
+				break;
+		}
+
 		status = detranslate_path(tracee, referee, referer);
 		if (status < 0)
 			break;
